---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="OpenAjang">
  <h1>OpenAjang</h1>
  <p class="lead">A small JSON format for publishing public events at a URL.</p>
  <p>
    Write an event file, link to your registration form, and host it on your own website or a static
    host such as GitHub Pages. Compatible apps and directories can read it, display it, and check for
    changes. There is no central service to join.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="/validator/">Validate an event file</a> ·
    <a href="/spec/">Read the specification</a> ·
    <a href="/examples/">Browse examples</a>
  </p>
  <h2>Status</h2>
  <p>
    Working draft, version 0.1. The schema is published at
    <a href="/schema/0.1/event.json"><code>/schema/0.1/event.json</code></a>, and the optional TypeScript
    SDK is on npm as <code>@openajang/core</code>.
  </p>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/nedpals/openajang#readme">Why this exists and how to publish your first event</a></p>
</Base>

<style>
  .lead { font-size: 1.25rem; }
</style>
